  "notes": "Source: official PFW Undergraduate Catalog, 'Program: Computer Science (B.S.) 4-Yr Plan', https://catalog.pfw.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=66&poid=18538&_ga=2.127149261.1907342208.1749755738-926849401.1749153023&print. The live catalog at catalog.pfw.edu is the 2025-2026 edition as of 2026-09-30, so catalog_year is 2025-2026 (current edition, not archived). Transcribed manually from the official term-by-term 4-year plan on 2026-09-30; course codes, titles, and credit values are exactly as published. CATALOG ANOMALY: the official plan lists MA 35100 (Elementary Linear Algebra, Cr. 3) in BOTH Spring 2nd Year and Fall 3rd Year. This appears to be a catalog error, but it is transcribed faithfully with a distinct code (MA 35100-2) for the second occurrence so the file passes pipeline duplicate-code validation; the credit sum follows the catalog's own arithmetic (120 total). The catalog also notes MA 51100 is accepted in place of MA 35100. Lab Science I and II are published as 4-5 credits each; both are modeled here at 4 credits (range documented in choice_note). 'Any electives to reach 120 credits' in Spring 4th Year is modeled at 2 credits so the semester/credit sums reconcile with the catalog's stated 120-credit total (catalog shows that term as '12+'). Prerequisite chains were NOT transcribed from the course-description pages, so every prereq array is empty and external_prereqs is empty; nothing was invented. Gen Ed category selections (B5/B6/B7/B8) are student choice slots; the catalog's own note reminds students to record completed categories. The four CS Concentration courses (12 credits total) are choice slots matching the catalog's concentration requirement.",
